{"name":"Blue Grey","hex":"#758da3","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue-grey","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of blue-gray."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of blue-gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue-grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Washington Crossing Council","blocks":[{"text":"Washington Crossing Council is a Scouting America council serving Pennsylvania’s Bucks County, and New Jersey’s Mercer and Hunterdon counties. The council was founded as Bucks County Council on August 13, 1928, and changed its name to Washington Crossing Council after receiving portions of the dissolved Central New Jersey Council."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/ad/Bucks_County_Council_CSP.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_Crossing_Council"},{"title":"Blue and Gray Museum (Georgia)","blocks":[{"text":"The Blue and Gray Museum in Fitzgerald, Georgia is located in a historic railroad depot that has been renovated to showcase the story of Fitzgerald's history and connections with the American Civil War. At the museum's core is its Hall of Honor, dedicated to the Civil War veterans who established the city. The museum also honors the town's local heroes, including General Raymond Gilbert Davis, the nation's most highly decorated Marine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/AB%26A_Historical_Train_Depot%2C_Fitzgerald.jpg/330px-AB%26A_Historical_Train_Depot%2C_Fitzgerald.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_and_Gray_Museum_(Georgia)"},{"title":"Blue-gray","blocks":[{"text":"Blue-gray is a medium blue-gray color on the cool side of the color wheel. The name blue-gray was introduced by Crayola for a crayon color used from 1958 to 1990. The complementary color is #CC9966, a warm khaki or brown."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue-gray"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c2/Ockanickon_Scout_Reservation.png/250px-Ockanickon_Scout_Reservation.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c2/Ockanickon_Scout_Reservation.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c2/Ockanickon_Scout_Reservation.png/250px-Ockanickon_Scout_Reservation.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOckanickon_Scout_Reservation.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Glacial_iceberg_in_Argentina.jpg/500px-Glacial_iceberg_in_Argentina.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Glacial_iceberg_in_Argentina.jpg/1280px-Glacial_iceberg_in_